From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:39:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Publish the web UI on 127.0.0.1 by default

The API has no authentication and GET /api/pull-secret/content returns
the pull secret, yet local-build.sh and mirror-gui.sh published the
port with -p "$WEB_PORT:$CONTAINER_PORT", which listens on every host
interface. On a shared bastion anyone who could reach the port could
read or replace the pull secret and start operations.

Both scripts now publish on WEB_BIND_ADDRESS, default 127.0.0.1
("localhost" is normalised to it, IPv6 addresses are bracketed for
Podman). Any other address prints a warning that the unauthenticated
API is reachable from the network. The README documents the variable
and SSH tunnelling for remote use.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019qihKhjEgccdwcruX2zHff
